				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">A force of about 14 or 15 SOK, Shady Lane and SSB met up today and vowed to bring down Krachenstein.
<br />

<br />
We had great healing and good support classes although I would have liked an extra tank or two. I wonder if a few Tank types are finding DAOC less fun nowadays, since the RVR aspect is more and more a Stealth or range game ? Either way we had two L50 champs and that proved to be enough.
<br />

<br />
Attempt number one didn't go right - since just as Erol was explaining the tactics I pulled Krach and ALL his guards down on top of us. I guess it just seemed the Jubal-like thing to do ?
<br />

<br />
So we went back for a second attempt. I split off from my group as instructed, still fully buffed, and happily pulled a guard and trotted back to the group. Sadly I pulled the whole lot again, which I didnt really notice until I got the whole group aggroed. Sigh. At least a rezzer logged, and we went for attempt number 3.
<br />

<br />
This time I logged out before pulling, and got no buffs at all. Slowly remembering some of the skills Lini and Leod taught me pulling Black Reavers in City of Mist, I pulled one guard away from the group. This time it worked, Verda peeled it off me - and one guard from 4 was down. Was great to hear someone say " Woot - he got one !".
<br />

<br />
A couple of pulls went bad as both times the guard or myself got too close to Krach - who teleported me next to him for a little private beatdown. However I avoided my earlier mistake by just finding a nice safe spot to die and be rezzed. Soon we had three of 4 guards dead. The fourth one was hard to get at - hiding all the way at the back, but I squirreled him out avoiding the big guy - so we got all 4.
<br />

<br />
After that Krach went down ok. We did get a nasty pop with 2 or 3 adds in the middle, but we killed the adds and then Krachenstein ok. 
<br />

<br />
Loot was disappointing. He dropped two things I think. Not sure what one was. One I won at the end was a 100% 1H Broadsword. Only 16.1 dps I think though with some nice stats but no proc and no glowy effect.
<br />

<br />
And that was largely it. One group of us explored the second level of Fomors - which was great because I had never seen it before. We killed loads and wandered across bridges and up ramps. In the end we met a second named Boss mob, who brought a couple of friends. We killed his friends ok, but he hid in the wall of the stairs we were on and just beat up on us form there. Awful pathing if you like - and it is going to be very hard to fight such a big mob on the stairs.
<br />

<br />
I had a great time - I think that was the best PvE I have had in ages. 
<br />
Many thanks to everyone from SOK, Shady Lane and SSB who took part, and I am sorry for the deaths. I am sure I can do it better next time.<br />_________________<br />Jagdar Singh L51 Celt Champion
<br />
Quicken Trueheart L48 Sylvan Valewalker
<br />
Jagdar Singh L54 Dark Elf Shadowknight(retired)
<br />
Sterling Order of Knights
<br />
"Why Zig and Zag, when you can Jag!"(tm)</span><span class="gensmall"></span></td>
